  "text" : "Now, the same week, something else, a paper, no press release, no front page, no journalist, it cuts the number of qubits you would need to break real encryption by roughly twenty times.\nThat isn't a supply story, it's arithmetic, and the arithmetic is already true.\nEvolution moves from 0.\n3 to 0.\n34.\nThe headline contributed one hundredth of that, the paper contributed the rest.\nWatch what it does.\nCrossing that line reprices everything.\nInsurance on this risk goes from just over a million pounds to 1.\n7 million.\nCaging it becomes literally impossible.\nNo cage tight enough exists to bring it inside the risk appetite.\nAnd fixing it, unchanged at £212,000, is suddenly the cheapest survivable move on the board.\nSo the Wargamer opens one signed pull request.\nStop insuring this, start fixing it, which is exactly right.\nYou cannot insure harvest now decrypt later.\nThe data is already stolen.\nIt is sitting on somebody's disk right now, encrypted, waiting."
